Z||000000||noyb||02-13-2001||04:05 PM||||Need to replace the steering column in my 86SE with an automatic transmission.  Someone told me that a steering column from a Grand Am would fit.  If this is true, is it limited to certain years for the Grand Am.  I will be posting a Grand Am brake question later.  Thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Larry Moss||02-13-2001||04:19 PM||||This reply may be a bit out of place, but for whatever it is worth, I once came across a fiero racing forum.  A driver with bouth a 1987 and `88 fiero, recommended, amoung other things, that 87 and earlier drivers, replace their races with a 1988 version.  It is supposed to make a difference.  <P>I do not know whether the swap is straight forward, but from the pictures, the 88 rack is the same length and shape as the 87 and earlier versiona.<P>I would really consider the 88 alternative before swapping out for another GM product.  In fact, I am not sure the other pontiac product will give you the results you desire, makes for a uncomplicated swap, or causes other issues.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||02-13-2001||07:36 PM||||He's talking about the column. not the rack....<P>the column can be taken from several other GM cars. I don't have a list handy. There are notes in my cave that you'll want to read before tearing it out.<A HREF="http://fierocave.shorturl.com" TARGET=_blank>The Ogre's Fiero Cave</A><P>You might have to change the column support bracket depending just what it came out of. Otherwise if it looks the same as the one in there now you should be fine. Take out the defective one so you can have it for comparison at the yard....||||reg||1
Z||000003||noyb||02-13-2001||08:48 PM||||Ogre.....I've read your article in the cave and the information is very valuable.  However, I have instant access to a Grand Am column, year unknown at the moment (80ish), and I'm looking for a definitive answer on the potential of this column fitting.  Or as definitive as I can get.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||02-14-2001||10:54 PM||||Pull the trim from under the Fiero and GA dashes. If the columns look the same they probably are. That is if the top section of both is round..... Some GMs are square between the wheel and dash.||||reg||1
